In article <2fqgq5$he5@scunix2.harvard.edu> mlevin@husc8.harvard.edu (Michael Levin) writes:

       I am running Ultrix 4.3 (rev. 44) and UWS 4.3 (rev. 10). All of a
   sudden I have noticed a few messages in my Session Manager window.
   They all read:

   Fixed up unaligned data access for pid 111 (dxterm) at pc 0x542120

   what could this mean?

It simply means that there is a non-fatal bug in dxterm; there are similar
bugs in Xws (X server under 4.3) and in other DECwindows software. The 
message simply says that the program accessed an unaligned memory location,
and that the access generated a trap and was fixed up by the kernel. You
could submit a bug report to DEC (yawn, shuffle, shuffle). 

BTW, I stopped using dxterm and switched to exclusive use of xterm
long time ago; recently I also threw out session manager and started
using xdm, because SM uses the not-so-good 'xhost' authorization scheme.
