> the audio port but I would like to play sound on an external
> speaker.  I am interested in info on DEC products or something I
> could piece together from Radio Shack-type parts.

	There is a little connector that plugs into the handset jack on
one end and has two subminature jacks on the other end.  The "speaker" end
can use any small speakers, such as those "self-powered" speakers commonly 
used with portable walkmans, other computer speakers, etc...  The "microphone"
is harder.  I've gotten good results by plugging in a "line-out" into the
microphone jack from a CD player or whatever to record from.

