Steve Gaarder (gaarder@well.sf.ca.us) wrote:
: I'm trying to integrate a Decstation 5000 model 50 running Ultirx 4.3A into
: our network and am having an automounter problem.  I can mount
: filesystems from Suna dn HP servers just fine, but when I try to access
: a filesystem on an SGI server (Irix 4.0.5) I get "permission denied."  I
: can mount the same filesystem with the mount command with no problems. 
: /usr/etc/automount -T gives the following output:

The problem is that SGI's have a secure automount deamon, looking for secure
requests.  Nothing but SGI's give that secure request that I've found.  There
is a very simple solution to the problem, just change the following lines
in the /usr/etc/inetd.conf file on the SGI and send a SIGHUP to inetd.  Change:


mountd/1    stream  rpc/tcp wait    root    /usr/etc/rpc.mountd     mountd
mountd/1    dgram   rpc/udp wait    root    /usr/etc/rpc.mountd     mountd

to

mountd/1    stream  rpc/tcp wait    root    /usr/etc/rpc.mountd     mountd -n
mountd/1    dgram   rpc/udp wait    root    /usr/etc/rpc.mountd     mountd -n


thats it.

Alan Palmer
apalmer@NMSU.edu




