   In article <JOHNS.93Dec20090922@haiti.gsfc.nasa.gov>, johns@haiti.gsfc.nasa.gov (Steve Johns) writes:
   |>For example, I need to do a "route add default <address>" command to
   |>ensure that a default route is defined in my routing table every time
   |>I boot.  Where should I put this command?  (Also, is there another way
   |>to get the system to do define this itself through one of the setup
   |>programs?)

   Create/edit a file called /etc/routes and place into one or more lines 
   of the form:

   net	gateway

   (For instance you could put in

   default	wan-gw

   which I what I use for my system).

In fact, if you use "netsetup" all this is done for you, as well as
setting up any other kind of routing you may want.  I find the
setup scripts that come with OSF really useful.


