DEC 3000/400 has a 133 MHz clock while DEC 3000/300 has a 150MHz clock.
Nonetheless DEC 3000/400 has more Specint92 because it has:
1) Wider internal buses.
2) More Caches.

So the 3000/400 is faster on a class of program that can't fit in the
the DEC 3000/300 caches. But if your program is more "local" like
probably 022.li you can have better performance with the DEC 3000/300
due to the faster clock.

For example if you look at the  Dhrystone bench you can see
			DEC 3000/300	DEC 3000/400	ratio
V1.1 (inst/sec)		327,439		287,356		113%
V1.2 (inst/sec)		287,522		256,805		119%
Clock MHz		150		133		113%
Specint92		58.2		65.5		88%
Specfp92		89.6		11.9		76%

These data are taken from a postscript file copied via anonymous ftp
from gatekeeper.dec.com. 
May be you can find other figure more up to date due to improvement
of the compiler.

