DEC has announced the TL820 storage box (or whatever it's officially
called - I work in engineering and often don't get the exact details
of a product's marketing.)

Anyway the box holds 288 TZ87 cartridges and 3 TZ87 drives. At 10Gbyte
per cartridge native, 20Gbyte w/2:1 compression, that's somewhere between
2.8 and 5 Tbyte per box. Up to 5 boxes can be interconnected.

The transfer rate is greater than 1 Mbyte/sec (native) per drive sustained
over the entire 10 Gbyte which gives you a 3.6 Gbyte/hour backup rate.
I don't know what the rate is for 3480 type cartridges is when expressed
in Gbyte/hr.

Interface to both drive(s) and robot controller is SCSI. There's several
options on what type of SCSI but I don't know exactly what's available so
I won't quote.

How your 2000 cartridges will map into 288 depends on how you want to
organize your data. It's probably not fair to compare total capacity to
total capacity. I suspect that you have a number of files that span
3480 cartridges that can be condensed into one TZ87 cartridge though.

