We are interested in buying a AXP 3000, specifically a model 600S some time
in the next six months.  However it seems to me that the Turbochannel about
which the current 3000s are built will soon be superceded by the PCI
'standard'.  In my inexpert opinion, the PCI bus is at least as fast as
TurboChannel (132Mb/sec burst V 100MB/sec).  If the PCI standard takes off,
as seems likely, then peripheral devices with this bus will be more
plentiful and cost less than similar Turbochannel devices.  In the longer
term Turbochannel will die.  PCI has also several operational advantages.

DEC seems to be moving to PCI, the next AXP 2000 machines will probably be
PCI.  DEC now has an Alpha chip with the PCI support logic inbuilt.  It is
just a matter of time.

I realise we can always wait for the latest and greatest, but I would hate
to recommend the purchase of the last Turbochannel based machine.

Any comments appreciated.

