FC is more focussed than ATM, because ATM vendors hope to unify all
types of communication (voice,video,data) and all distribution
categories (LAN, long haul). FC, in contrast, stretches all the way
to SCSI-3 and HIPPI. Different markets.

The ATM argument is that packetizing allows users to buy different
data rates, and mostly Not Have To Know how fast or slow some faraway
link is going. Which is why cheap silicon for ATM may show up at 54
Mb/s, clearly not a Cray-level product.
