In article <52gZDc1w165w@gold.muc.de>, mws@gold.muc.de (Markus Spring) writes:
> I am using DECImageScan Software V3.0 which produces .img, .ddif or
> (large...) .ps-Files. I would like to import scanned graphics into
> WordPerfect, which knows a lot of graphics formats, but not those
> created by DECScan.
> Is there an Converter, which is able to handle A4-Size 300dpi Scans or 
> do I really have to go to a PC to produce WP-readable scans?

	The CDA Converter Library (Yes, an additional product) thinks it
can convert the image from DDIF to TIFF.  However, it doesn't write the
tag for "fillorder" correctly.  It can be fixed using PATCH/ABSOLUTE
after you convert the image.  It goes something like this:

	$ CONVERT IMAGE.DDIF/FORMAT=DDIF IMAGE.TIF/FORMAT=TIFF
	$ PATCH/ABSOLUTE IMAGE.TIF
	PATCH> DEPOSIT 66
	PATCH> 1
	PATCH> EXIT
	PATCH> UPDATE
	PATCH> EXIT
	$ !... all done

> mws@gold.muc.de (Markus Spring) 
