We upgraded a network of Suns to Alphas a year ago and have no major
horror stories to report.

I have found DEC support to be pretty good but I can only vouch for the
UK.  At least they are still interested in the Edu market - other
vendors don't seem to care any more.

Optimisation is not great but it has got much better between releases,
as has the whole OS.  For benchmark speed though KAP must be used.

Performance is great - not just in speed but also in managing a
multi-user environment.  We normally have three of four jobs on the
alphas and the sessions hardly notice.  This does require some kernel
tuning, though.

Third party applications etc - as with all new machines they take a
little bit of time to come along.  Porting stuff to it though is very
easy.  Having less games ported to alphas does have its' advantages...

Unless there is some very specific software that you want to use that
hasn't been ported yet, I can't think of any reasons for not buying an
alpha. 


