As for the DSP5400, it must be realized that it is a 4 GB drive,
which is larger than ULTRIX can support in a single partition.
Once ULTRIX supports drives this large it will do so by not 
having a single partition span the entire disk.  Most likely
C will be the first 2.1 GB and some other the rest.

The default partition table on the other hand may still have
C be the entire disk.  When this is the case, the disk will
have to be repartitioned so that no single partition is larger
than the 2 GB limit.

