HIPPI and SCI need not be more expensive. You might consider, that fast ICs are 
already built in BiCMOS and offer ECL input/output at NO additional costs.

Using ECL as I/O simplifies power supply, ground layout and ground shields, 
as:
	- currents through all drivers sum up to a constant!
		therefor no ground bounce 
	- signals are differential, thereby immune to ground bounce ;-<>
	- drivers drive 50 Ohm load easily, you may design your system
		according to RF standards. (terminated lines etc. etc ...)
	- radio interference is hardly a problem with direfferential ECL-lines

