[extracted...]
> Opening a DecTerm window there is a problem when scrolling up and down:  if you
> stretch the window (so that you can see more of the previous lines) and then
> move up and down, the upper part of the screen does not get updated.  Someone
> told me that this is something I should be able to fix,  but I haven't figured
> out how.
> 

You can partially fix this problem by setups in the Decterm 'Options' menu.

1.  Select Window...
2.  Make sure that the 'Auto Resize Terminal', 'Auto Resize Window',
    and 'Terminal Driver Resize' options are all selected.
3.  Select 'Save Options'.

The Decterm window will correctly update when you make it larger (in height
or width).  However, if you make the window smaller, text which is clipped
off in the smaller window appears to be totally lost.

This fix seems to work equally well for Decstations running OSF-1 or
Vaxstations running VMS.
