> Is anyone currently using a Digital DSP 3160 [1.6 Gb] drive under
>Ultrix 4.3?  I'm looking for an fstab entry.

I think you mean "disktab".  The fstab entry would look something
like:

/dev/rz1c:/mnt/disk:rw:1:2:ufs::

As for the disktab entry, you don't need one.  Since ULTRIX V4.0
newfs(8) (or mkfs(8)) has been smart enough to ask the drive
its geometry and size.  If you want to partition the drive, then
create a small file system on A, repartition and use whatever
partitions you want.  If you just want the whole disk, use C.

The form of the command to have newfs/mkfs get the geometry is:

# newfs /dev/rrz#x /dev/rrz#x

