True today.  However, three to five years from now, one or more of the cooling
fans will probably fail.  If the machine is used in a room containing dozens
of other cooling fans (all whining at slightly different pitches), you
usually notice a fan failure the hard way; like when your machine suddenly
pukes and dies.

It might be a good idea to provide some sort of warning if the cooling fans
fail and the interior of the system enclosure begins to heat up.  The user
might be notified by some sort of alarm light or beeper.  Also, the operating
system software might be notified, so the system can be automatically shut
down.  Perhaps a thermostat on the processor heatsink might work ??
