DECnet is a protocol that runs over ethernet.  
TCP/IP is a protocol that runs over ethernet.
CAP is a unix program that sends iptalk (encapsulated
Appletalk, i.e. on Ethernet) datagrams over ethernet
and maintains analogs of MAC file structure on a
unix machine.  I just got a brochure from PACER
619-454-0565, pacesetter@pacersoft.com showing
Macintosh to VMS file and print server software.
I don't know much about it, though.  As far as ethernet
interfaces for the Macintosh,  if you don't need the
speed,  consider a Shiva Fastpath localtalk to ethernet
box.  IMHO, Ethernet speed is needed if you want to put
shared applications on the server, however.
Good luck.


