    One activity that will help is to INITIALIZE your news disk with
    /HEADERS=nnnnn, where 'nnnnn' is about twice the maximum number of
    files that willl be stored on the disk.  If you do restore files from
    BACKUP, be sure to specify /NOINITIALIZE, so the extra file headers
    will remain.

    If the standard deviation of file sizes is small, you might also change
    the cluster size on the news disk to be slightly higher than the average
    file size.

    You might also increase the size of the File ID Cache (ACP_FIDCACHE),
    the File Header Cache (ACP_HDRCACHE), the Directory Cache (ACP_DIRCACHE),
    and the number of file windows (ACP_WINDOW).



