The thermal characteristics of the 21064 package are *very* good, 
having evolved from (actually, along side) the package developed for the 
NVAX (e.g. VAX4000-400/500/600, etc). This helps ease the demands on the
heatsink a little. The 21064 in the DECpc AXP 150 is rather strongly
overcooled at 150MHz, because we decided to use a heatsink that had already
been designed for another project rather than design a new one (what Bob
Supnik affectionately refers to as "the Briggs&Stratton heatsink"). One would 
have to do a little analysis (maybe it's already been done) to see what the
thermal issues would be in another box, but my gut says that the cooling
of the 21064 is much less of a problem than the cooling of the linear
regulator
that supplies +3.3V to the chip (at least in the DECpc design).

..tom


