> I'm trying to send mail to my sister at Gaulledet University in DC,
> and they are using VAX machines.
>
> She gave me a email address as GALLUD||CLIN
>
> I can't send emails with pipes in them since I"m sending it from the SUN.
>
> How can I send her emails and how can I receive emails?

    No solution, but some comments that may or may not help:

        1) GALLUD||CLIN is NOT a valid (vanilla) VMS e-mail
           address.  Are you sure she didn't say GALLUD::CLIN ?
           The `::' syntax specifies a DECnet node.  You'd need DECnet
           on the Sun, (which is available if not too common), or a
           gateway from your Sun to DECnet.

        2) You should ask your sister if GALLUD:: is running any
           form of TCP/IP.  She'll probably have to ask her system
           manager or the HELP desk.  If it is, then get the correct
           Internet node and domain from her and use an Internet
           style address to send her mail.  Most VMS systems that
           can _receive_ Internet mail can send it from the vanilla
           VMS MAIL interface just using the REPLY command within
           MAIL.  She'll need to pay attention to the From: field
	   and use that specification if she wants to SEND...

        -Ken
