I just sent this to the GCC bug report address.  Perhaps someone here
has some input on this problem as well...

This problem has been demonstrated on a DEC MIPS box running Ultrix 4.3,
and on an SGI MIPS box running IRIX 4.0.5, with GCC 2.4.5 and 2.5.5.

Compile the following program:

	#include <exception.h> 
	main()
	{
		printf("hello world, proc table = 0x%ld\n",_procedure_table);
	}

with GCC.  The native loader (/bin/ld) will dump core.

The following workaround has been discovered:

> If you take every object file produced by gcc (after the tfile conversion)
> and run it through the native mips linker (without gcc intervention), it
> seems to clean up whatever mess gcc made:
> 
>       /usr/bin/ld -r -o junk.o foo.o
>       mv junk.o foo.o
> 

